TEXT:
CSRU Nursing Update
Neuro: Pt lethargic throughout day, requires frequent stimulation; TSH sent, ABG's followed; Flat affect; Oriented to place, time, person; PERL; OOB to chair during day, ambulated; MAE, slightly weak;
CV: Pt in sinus rhythm w/frequent PAC's, occais PVC's; A paced through most of day-pacer currently AAI back up; BP stable-neo off-see carevue flowsheet; Generalized edema; Skin cool to touch; Pulses dopplered;
Resp: Pt currently on 6 liters NC; Lungs cl bilat; Resps labored w/activity; Sats 96 or better; ABG shows low P02, nl PH; Weak cough; uses IS to 750 cc;
GI: Active BS, poor appetite, frequently falling asleep during meals; Abd soft, obese;
GU: Foley in place, urine output adequate, on lasix [**Hospital1 **];
SKin: Groin ecchymotic; Abd binder to prevent wound dehisce; Ace wrap to R leg;
Pain: Denies pain-narcotics held d/t lethargy;
Endo: Covering glucose per sliding scale
Plan: Cont pulm toilet, Review TSH result; Neuro checks, monitor hemodynamics;

CSRU Nursing Update
Neuro: Alert and oriented x3; MAE w/good strength; PERL; found attempting to get OOB alone ~4am-placed in chair;
CV: Pt in afib, freq PVC's; BP stable-see carevue flow sheet; Pacer wires in place, secured; Pulses palpable; Skin warm and dry;
Resp: currently on 4 liters NC-5l NC overnight; Sats 94 or better, slightly sob w/activity; Lungs cl bilat; Wet cough; IS to 1000;
GI: Active BS, drank clears overnight; Abd soft, obese
GU: Voids in Bedside commode adequate amounts-on Lasix-IV BID;
Pain: Denies pain;
Activity: OOB to commode/chair;
Labs: Difficulty obtaining adequate amount of blood for PT-pt refusing Venipuncture;
Plan: cont activity; Obtain PT if possible; Transfer to [**Hospital Ward Name **] 2;

Respiratory Care;

during the day shift the RN was nice enough to do her neb. Rx's.
She seems to be doing well post NIPPV.

npn 13:00

(see careview flow-notes)

neuro:
     adequately sedated on 30 mcg/hr fentanyl; received bolus x2 for discomfort with noxious cares;
     opens eyes spontaneously at times, to voice at times, localizes stimuli;  does not appear distressed though with low levels of sedation re intubation/ventilation;
     extremities remain flaccid;

c-v:
     sbp 130's-150's; HR afib to 120's at beginning of shift, down to 110's after diltiazam of 10:00, then down to 88-90's after 12:00 dose of increased dose of lopressor (75 mg from 50);
     continues to have [**2-13**]+ edema; received Lasix 160 mg IV at approx 10:30, with excellent diuretic effect of at least 500cc/hr for 3 hrs following;
     resolution of sepsis s/p Abx and decrease of sedation likely contributing to autodiuresis as well;

heme:  a.m. hct 28.1, (above goal of 28);

resp:
     remains intubated d/t GI issues and assist ventilation/prevent atelectasis re likely resolving sepsis; possibility yet of endoscopy, attending MD [**First Name (Titles) 16**] [**Last Name (Titles) **] MD continue to discuss case and interventional plan;
     PS 10/PEEP 10/FIO2 40%; suctioned q1-2 hrs for sm amt whitish return; at 08:00 orally suctioned for Copious amount whitish opaque return;  O2 sat 100% most of the day;

g-i:
     abd baseline excessive obesity; [**Last Name (Titles) **] feeds remain on hold for further GI interventional plan;
     receiving free H2O and meds via OGT;
     free H2O increased from 250 cc q6 to 500cc q6 secondary to hypernatremia--seems a very large volume for each administration; divided into 250cc q 3 hrs, will discuss with MD/team;
     08:00 FS 169, insulin gtt resumed, FS done q 1-1 1/2 hr until in therapeutic goal (80-120);
     continues to have mush cath, draining dark brown liquid stool;

g-u:  urine qs, diuresis discussed aboved, via patent foley;

i.d.  afebrile so far today; a.m. WBC 6.5;

access: continues with Lft [**First Name9 (NamePattern2) **] [**Last Name (un) **] CVL, recently changed over wire [**2-20**];  LFt rad A-Line patent;

skin:  on rotating bari-bed for automatic position changes secondary; to pt's morbid obesity; duoderms intact;

social:  oldest daughter called approx 10:00, updated;

Disposition:  62 y/o blk female, initially admitted for Bright red rectal bleeding/GIB, s/p PEA arrest x2 while hospitalized, A-fib w/ RVR, sepsis causing hypotension, difficulty weaning from ventilator;

Full Code
Family meeting/communication for plan re ?trach;

Plan:
1)  follow fluid balance
2)  pt to receive 2nd dose 160 mg IV Lasix tonight approx 22:00
3)  no new plan re ventilation
4)  follow T
5)  cont to hld [**Month/Year (2) **] feeds until GI plan
6)  FS's/insulin gtt to obtain FS between 80-120
7)  pt to receive PICC line in preparation for placement

npn 7p-7a:

dx: w/u GIB, s/p PEA x2, rapid A-fib, DM, depression, morbid obesity;

NEURO:
     remains off sedation; alert at beginning of shift, + eye tracking, less responsive later in the shift when turned for hygiene cares;  moves upper extremities spont, no mvt observed LE's;

CV:
     on amiodarone, diltiazam, and lopressor for b/p and hrt rate control;  lopressor increased to TID last eve;  continues to have generalized edema, last received lasix yest 11:00;

RESP:
     on RA at beginning of shift, O2 sat's 95-98%, appeared comfortable, RR 16-20; put on bi-pap at HS to assist expand of alveoli; O2 sat 98-99% overnoc;

GI:
     on peptamen [** **]-feeds, no resid via ogt, placement checked x3; continues to have rectal mushroom cath for liquid dark brown-green stool;

GU:
     urine output qs via foley; recieved 500 cc free H20 q 6 hrs, via
ogt;

SKIN:
     duoderms on back patent; on bari-bed to relieve pressure points re severe obesity and bedrest;

ACCESS:
     Lt [**First Name9 (NamePattern2) 10134**] [**Last Name (un) **] CVL with 1 port clotted; Lt A-Line patent;

Disposition:
     1)  start preparing for transfer to rehab
     2)  will need PICC placement for rehab
     3)  follow serum Na+ level
     4)  adv [**Last Name (un) **] feeds

npn 2a

dx:  w/u for GIB, s/p PEA x2

neuro:
off all sedation; reponsive, eyes open spont, + eye tracking; purposeful upper extremity movement;

c-v:
on amnio, lopressor, diltiazam; sbp 150's-170's;

resp:  on 2 l nc O2, O2 sats 98-99%; at HS placed on nasal bi-pap, tolerating well, O2 sat 95-7%; lungs diminshed, with occs'l wheeze; receiving nebbs via resp therapy;

g-i:
[** **] feeding increased to 60 cc/hr at 8p with good toleration, turned off at 12 MN d/t planned speech and swallow eval Monday;

f/e:  continues to received 500 cc free H2O q 4 hrs for hypernatremia, also receives daily lasix;

endo:  insulin gtt not changed yesterday, therefor received new insulin sliding scale aftef MN FS (273);

g-u:  urine output adeq via patent foley; currently ordered to received daily lasix (160 mg);

skin:  duoderms patent to sites on back

i.d.:  continues to be afebrile;

plan:

1)  n-pap overnoc, maintain seated position;
2)  free H2O, daily lasix as ordered
3)  swallow eval at bedside Monday
4)  PICC line placement Mon
5)  trasition to NPH insulin when taking PO
6)  pt to sit upright overnight secondary to obstructive lung dz d/t morbid obesity
7)  FS's q b hrs w/ riss coverage

npn 5a addendum:

re a.m. labs:

hct>28 (29.2); wbc nl @ 9.2;
Na+ 142, K+ nl, both calcium and phos serum levels below nl;
coags without significant change or values;

assessment: 1)  hypernatremia resolved;
     2)  afebrile with nl WBC despite off Abx for a few days;
     3)  may need calcium and phos supplementation
     4)  stable hct

npn 3p-7p

neuro/resp:  pt more responsive at 18:00 after removal of face mask bi-pap; d/w resp therapist who stated pt reportedly did not get much sleep last night and wanted to sleep today;  did not respond much when PICC line placed at 17:25;
     placed on 2 l nc;  O2 sats 100%;

c-v:  b/p w/in pts range on amio, lopressor, diliazem

g-i:  NGT placement checked, [** **] feeding rate increased to 45 cc/hr, goal 75 cc/hr;

g-u:  urine output remains adequate;

access:  PICC line placed left a.c. via interventional radiology at 17:25, post placement p-cxr showed tip in jugular; int rad returned 18:30 to revise placement; p-cxr ordered;

plan:  1)  MD to check 2nd p-cxr
   2)  advance [** **] feed to goal as [** **]
   3)  bi-pap overnoc again
   4)  a.m. labs
   5)  pt to remain in sitting position re lung limitation d/t morbid obesity
   6)  d/c planning

npn 3p-7p (completion of note for 7a-7p)

addendum:

neuro/social:  pt combative to RNs a few times, male attendant stated pt aggitated/combative to females at times, stated some female caregivers at the facility refuse to care for him;

resp: former trach site suctioned again for sm amt whitish return; no new issues;

social:  sister in again this eve, updated of pt status;

Disposition: to stay in MICU-A overnoc, probable transfer out tomorrow

npn 7a-3p

see careview flowsheet

neuro: pt w/ baseline hx MR, lives at facility; alert, non-verbally coomunicative via nods and facial expressions; care facility attendant with pt at all times, assists w/ communicating w/ pt; moves extremities spont and w/ purpose, though baseline limited;

c-v:  b/p stable today, good urine output; o2 sat adequate; JP drains x2 with small amount drainage;

resp:  O2 sat 98-100% on FIO2 50% trach mist mask; [**Last Name (un) 10598**] sounds ess clear bil w/ good air movement; resp rate 18, no accessory muscle usage; trach site sxn'd x2-3 for sm-mod amt secretions;

ID:  on IV Abx; on MRSA precautions, also hx of c-diff (no diarrhea at this time);

g-i:  tube feeds resumed, increased from 40 to 50 cc/hr, goal 70 cc/hr; abd soft, + bwl sounds;

social: sister in at noon; NM from residential facility called today to check on pt

pain: facial grimace and restless/anxious  behaviors w/ pain, recieved 5 ml oxycodone w/ acet. elixir x2, pt appeared comfortable both times following absorption;

g-u:  urine output large via foley, brighter yellow following absorption of vitamins;

npn 7p-7a  (please see careview flownotes for objective data)

dx:
s/p whipple procedure
s/p thoracentesis
GIB

neuro:
appeared confused/dazed at beginning of this shift; pt also noted to be s/p versed for procedure yesterday;a/o mid-way through the night; stated she "doesn't want anymore", stated "I'm in misery", denied pain, stated "mental misery";
   pt's sister [**Name (NI) 852**] is Health Care proxy; will need to allow pt and pt's sister to make decisions for pt's care;

c-v:
sbp 130's-140's last eve, up to 160's after blood transfusions (2 units) last eve; b/p did trend downward, below goal of 130 at approx 04:30, therefore pt received LR 500 cc bolus from approx 05:00-06:00, pt's b/p returned to sbp 140;
   hct 33.2 after 2 units PRBC's last night; at 04:00 hct 31.0; transient hypotension w/ slight increase in hrt rate and 2.0 pt decrease in hct suggests pt still g-i bleeding;

g-i:
no bloody or melanous secretions from pt's mouth this night; only one melanous stool at 23:00,soft formed, moderate to large size;
   remains on TPN for nutrition; FS's adequate;

g-u:
urine output decreased to insufficient at approx same time as lower b/p and slightly higher hrt rate; addressed w/ LR 500 cc IV bolus as stated;

skin:
pt w/ much generalized edema; at risk for breakdown, though no breakdown d/t pressure/positioning;
  rt mid-quad incision intact w/ staples; JP drain draining small amount dark greenish/melana stained fluid;
   LFt wrist A-line drssg changed d/t slight drainage; mult-[**Last Name (un) 1389**] CVL site intact;

ID:
afebrile, however WBC still rising;

resp:
using Face tent mist, O2 sats ususually 96-98%;

PLAN:
1) keep sbp >130
2) transfusions PRN
3) abx
4) pt and pt's sister to direct her plan of care

npn 7p-7a addendum:

re skin:
pt with Rt heel non-blanching redness approx size 50 cent piece,  present at admission; now with developing darkness in the center despite positioning on pillow to prevent further injury;

NPN 7p-7a  (please see careview flownotes for objective data)

dx:  CA; s/p whipple; s/p bilat thoracentesis;
     GIB

neuro:
alert, states she "wants to go"; states she "doesn't want any more";
pt's sister [**Name (NI) 852**], [**Name (NI) 6596**] Care Proxy states pt desires to die; pt with purposeful movement;

c-v:
no episodes of hypotension this night; tachy low 120's at beginnning of shift, recieved lopressor IV 5 mg, to assist w/ hrt rate control (prevent Beta blocker rebound effect from abrupt cessation); did not drop blood pressure at all, but was effective in decreasing hrt rate;
hct stable this night;

resp:
remains on 4 l nc plus face tent-- on loosely per pt preferency;

g-i:
NPO except Carafate; no [**Location (un) 6597**] stained secretions from mouth, however continues to have thick melanous stool;

g-u/electrolytes;
urine output adequate, though on low side; color amber;

skin;
rt mid quadrant surgical incision site with staples and patent J-P drain--draining dark, melanous stained fluid;

ID:
afebrile overnight; however WBC still elevated; remains on IV Abx;

PLAN:
[**Hospital 103**] health care proxy, sister--[**Name (NI) 852**], to discuss plan of care for pt;
remainder of plan unchanged at this time.

npn 7p-7a  (also see careview flownotes for objective data)

dx:  s/p whipple; s/p bilat thoracentesis
     new GIB

neuro:
lethargic at times, alert/awake at times; verbalizations limited to repeated single word expressions, ex. "hurry"; "hurry up";  remains very weak, very little extremity movement;

c-v:
b/p stable, within normal limits; hct also stable this night, though slightly down (2 pts) at 03:00; very little old black stool this night via rectal bag;  hrt rate 84 at lowest, usually in 90's; often in low 100's; NSR w/ rare PAC's; pedal pulses by dopplar; excessive generalized edema;

resp:
continues to use n.c. O2 plus mist mask; O2 sats 96-98%; respirations shallow, rate 24-33; lungs sounds diminished at bases;

g-i:
abd very distended, much anascara; Rt mid quad incision intact w/ staples, leaks dark green fluid at times; JP drain draining dark green fluid, less melanous tinged than previous two nights; as stated, very little old dark black stool via rectal bag;

g-u:
urine color more med yellow this night than dark amber of past 3 nights; volume also improved, despite no fluid boluses; folwy patenet;

skin:
no pressure sores; is leaking anascara fluid from tissues onto bedding, requires frequent hygiene care;

access:
a-line with brief period of inaccuracy both last night and tonight with affected wave form; line flushed, wrist repositioned, tracing returned to nl;

social;
sister present this eve again; states pt desires/ready to die;

PLAN:
1) hct checks per team; resident to call attending if PRBC transfusion is to be considered;
2) hygiene cares
3) provide optimal comfort for pt
4) pt DNR/DNI at this time

npn 7p-7a (see also carevue flownotes for objective data)

dx: refractory trigeminal neuralgia


Pt here for lidocaine gtt treatment for Trig. neuralgia; is hoped Lidocaine would interfere with receptor sites for nerve pain sensation process;

vss; pt w/out new complaints;
Lidocaine remains at 75 mg/hr; pt received supplemental magnesium PO as ordered;

Pt a/o x3, communicative with care-givers/staff; stands at side of bed to use commode independently without issue;
   did have one episode of ST to 130 when standing at side of bed, pt w/out complaints at that time;

PLAN:
1) pt in [**Wardname **]4 ICU until Lidocaine gtt complete
2) pain service making recoomendations for treatment of pt's trig neuralgia pain
3) anticipate pt's needs
4) d/c to floor when off lidocaine gtt
